  background: #cec3d4;
  border-radius: 50%;
  font-size: 0.4rem;
  height: 7em;
  width: 7em;
  margin-bottom: 2rem;
  position: relative;
  /*  HOW THIS WORKS
  	There is a background circle that is always the incomplete color. 2 layers (both half circles) are used to create the completed fill.

  	0-50%:	Top layer colors the left side as the incomplete color (bottom layer is hidded by this). The top layer remains fixed.
  			Bottom layer is the working color (starts on the left and rotates 0-180 degrees) 
  	51-99%:	The top layer is flipped to cover the right side and it's color is changed to the working color
  			Bottom layer continues to be rotated through 181-360 degrees
  	100%	Top layer is on the right and appears in the completed color
  			Bottom layer is on the left and appears in the completed color 
  */
